---
description: Platform and workspace architecture
alwaysApply: true
---

Place code in the lowest-level package that owns the concept and satisfies its platform requirements.

Package responsibilities:

- `tinker-chest`: platform-agnostic utilities and primitives
- `ui/common`: shared UI components and primitives
- `ui/web`: web-specific UI components and styling
- `ui/mobile`: mobile-specific UI components and styling
- `apparatus/common`: shared application logic and state
- `apparatus/web`: web-specific application logic and integrations
- `apparatus/mobile`: mobile-specific application logic and integrations
- `gears/*/common`: shared plugin logic
- `gears/*/web`: web-specific plugin logic
- `gears/*/mobile`: mobile-specific plugin logic
- `app-web`: web application composition and entry points
- `app-mobile`: mobile application composition and entry points

Keep application packages focused on composition, wiring, and platform concerns.

Keep reusable logic and state in lower-level packages.

Only share code when behavior is genuinely platform-independent.

Prefer duplication over incorrect abstraction.